Subject: Commercial Auto / Trucking Insurance – Address Clustering Analysis Highlighting Potential Risk Concentration

To Underwriting, SIU, and Claims Leadership,

I am providing a dataset of ${cluster_count} address clusters involving FMCSA-registered motor carriers (representing over ${"{:,}".format(total_carriers)} individual USDOT authorities) that exhibit characteristics which may represent elevated or misrepresented risk.

While many of the structures identified (use of registered agents, virtual offices, etc.) are legally permissible, they can obscure the true operational footprint and risk profile of the insureds. Insurers ultimately bear the cost of claims arising from these arrangements.

Notable patterns in the attached data include:
- High volumes of inactive authority concentrated at single addresses
- Physical locations that are PO Boxes, virtual offices, or have no visible trucking operations
- Apparent front companies or aggregator models with very high turnover of individual operators
- Clusters where the listed physical address does not appear consistent with the scale of reported power units

The attached TSV includes carrier counts, active/inactive power unit data, and specific notes for each cluster. I have highlighted entries where the physical address appears to be a virtual office, mail service, or residential location, as these may warrant additional underwriting scrutiny or verification of actual operations.

This analysis is offered as an informational resource. I am happy to discuss methodology or provide further detail.

